<http://data.silknow.org/object/00df0e77-77ea-37a7-82f8-58ec5429f9fb>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Pair of shoes for a child, made of plaited straw and catgut, lined with red silk.  The shoes are heel-less with rounded square toes, and are in a slip-on style with no fastenings or adjustment.  They  are made in a striped openwork pattern, each with a rosette on the vamp."@en , "Shoes for a child, plaited straw and horsehair, lined with red silk; made in England, 1850-1870"@en ;
